title: The Knives Come Out
tags: event
priority: 3
view-if: con_in_government = 0 and defeated_once = 1 and in_campaign = 0 and time - leadership_challenge_time >= 12 and (thatcher_rating < 35 or dissent >= 0.3)
new-page: true
on-arrival: leadership_challenge_time = time
face-image: img/events/heath_thatcher.jpg

= The Knives Come Out

After the defeat, the 1922 Committee has agreed to a leadership election. Edward Heath's friends are canvassing, and Francis Pym has been sounded out.

- @fight: Stand for re-election as leader.
- @concessions: Offer the wets a share of the leadership.
- @resign: Stand down.

@fight
on-arrival: {!
var support = 62 + 0.6 * (Q.thatcher_rating - 30) - 30 * (Q.dissent - 0.2) + (Q.con_votes - Q.lab_votes);
Q.challenge_support = Math.round(support);
Q.survived = (support + (Math.random() - 0.5) * 12 >= 50) ? 1 : 0;
!}
go-to: survived if survived = 1; ousted if survived = 0

@concessions
on-arrival: {!
Q.wet_dissent -= 15;
Q.dry_dissent += 10;
Q.economic_liberalism -= 3;
var support = 68 + 0.6 * (Q.thatcher_rating - 30) - 30 * (Q.dissent - 0.2) + (Q.con_votes - Q.lab_votes);
Q.challenge_support = Math.round(support);
Q.survived = (support + (Math.random() - 0.5) * 12 >= 50) ? 1 : 0;
!}
go-to: survived if survived = 1; ousted if survived = 0

You promise a broader front bench and a gentler economic message.

@survived
on-arrival: wet_dissent -= 5; loyalist_dissent -= 8; thatcher_rating += 4

You win, not overwhelmingly, but clearly enough to end the talk of a second round. You will lead the party into the next election.

@ousted
on-arrival: ousted = 1
go-to: game_over

The party turns to a gentler, more familiar kind of leader. Your time as leader is over.

@resign
on-arrival: ousted = 1
go-to: game_over

You announce that you will not stand. The party will choose a new leader.

@healey
title: Callaghan Retires
tags: event
view-if: con_in_government = 0 and defeated_once = 1 and time >= 35 and lab_leader == "Callaghan"
max-visits: 1
new-page: true
on-arrival: lab_leader = "Healey"; prime_minister = "Healey"; lab_leader_rating = 46
face-image: img/events/healey.jpg

= Callaghan Retires

James Callaghan, nearly seventy, has retired. Labour MPs have chosen Denis Healey to succeed him as Prime Minister, by a comfortable margin over Michael Foot. Healey is formidable, combative and respected in the markets. He will be harder to beat than Callaghan.

@labour_winter
title: Another Winter of Strikes
tags: event
view-if: con_in_government = 0 and defeated_once = 1 and strike_wave >= 5 and labour_winter_seen = 0
max-visits: 1
new-page: true
on-arrival: labour_winter_seen = 1; labour_credibility -= 6; lab_leader_rating -= 6; union_backlash += 6
face-image: img/events/winter_of_discontent_2.jpg

= Another Winter of Strikes

Labour's incomes policy has broken down again. The public-sector unions are out, and the newspapers reprint the photographs of 1979. Your case that only the Conservatives can deal with the unions has never been stronger.

@labour_snap
title: Labour Calls an Election
tags: event
view-if: con_in_government = 0 and defeated_once = 1 and months_since_election >= 42 and lab_votes >= con_votes + 2 and election_called = 0 and in_campaign = 0
max-visits: 1
new-page: true
on-arrival: time_to_election = 2
call: set_election
face-image: img/events/westminster.jpg

= Labour Calls an Election

With Labour ahead in the polls, [+ lab_leader +] goes to the Palace. The general election will be held in [+ next_election_month : month +] [+ next_election_year +].
